{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3027","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3027","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3027\",\"parent_revision\":\"2af71e6e0ceb582d488f3badb67ab47c591bd57aaec3591083cbb6f95ae5be91\",\"root_revision\":\"2af71e6e0ceb582d488f3badb67ab47c591bd57aaec3591083cbb6f95ae5be91\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMultiple agents/PRs touching the same plugin (development-harness) concurrently each bump\\nplugin.json to the same next version independently. Observed twice in one session on PR #3015:\\nmain landed #3023 bumping dh 9.0.16->9.0.17, then #3024 bumping 9.0.17->9.0.18, each time\\ncolliding with this branch's own already-committed bump to the identical number.\\n\\ncheck_plugin_version_bump.py --check --base-ref origin/main then reports \\\"changed but did not\\nbump\\\" even though a bump commit exists, because the two sides converged on the same version\\nnumber by coincidence, not by ancestry. auto_sync_manifests.py's pre-commit hook cannot\\nself-heal this since it only diffs the staged git index, not origin/main, so it has no way to\\ndetect a post-rebase collision.\\n\\nNeeds either:\\n(a) a rebase-time or push-time check that detects \\\"version unchanged after rebase but content\\n    differs from the version-bump commit's parent\\\" and auto-re-bumps, or\\n(b) a coordination mechanism (e.g. a reserved/monotonic version counter, or a CI job that\\n    auto-bumps-and-pushes on collision) so agents stop needing to manually re-bump plugin.json\\n    every time a sibling PR lands the same plugin's bump on main first.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **plugin.json version-bump race under concurrent agents/prs** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #3015 session, 2026-08-19\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5c772c9fe01156cb47d79898fdaa1ca3ffaf26c14b1f3f9aeb74bd37c27cb962\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnFcTQ\"}"}